On Wed, 20 Oct 2004, Stephen Rothwell wrote:
> Thanks to Wolfgang Denk I have recovered (some of) the old list archives.
> Please see http://ozlabs.org/pipermail/linuxppc-dev/
> 
> I don't know how complete the archive is ...

This inspired me too (finally) take a look at my email archives on CDR.

Below is the list of all archives. Right now they're in pure mailbox
format and may contain some mails not sent to the mailing lists, but I
can filter them up and export them (pine export) to files per month,
without unneeded headers.

They cover the following mailing lists (doh, I didn't even remember we
used to have a list at Motorola :-):

  - linux-ppc@meetpoint.mcu.motsps.com
  - linuxppc-dev@cs.wisc.edu
  - linuxppc-dev@lists.linuxppc.org
  - linuxppc-user@lists.linuxppc.org
  - linuxppc-announce@lists.linuxppc.org
  - linuxppc-workstation@lists.linuxppc.org
  - linuxppc-bk@fsmlabs.com
  - linuxppc-commit@hq.fsmlabs.com

Stephen, if you want (some of these) to be archived at ozlabs, let me
know which ones, and I'll spend some time on it...

